  "ai": {
    "status": "ok",
    "model": "deepseek-chat",
    "summary": "This PR only touches .github/workflows/ci.yml and the decision preview is REVIEW, not an approval. The report shows a single Ready worker with 2190m CPU and ~9.2 GB memory available, but 35 unreserved container requests mean free capacity is likely overstated, and a KubeCPUOvercommit warning is firing. The trusted worker-capacity case confirms the control-plane node is tainted and must not be counted as schedulable worker capacity, so effective headroom is smaller than the raw numbers suggest. The change itself is a workflow pin change with no manifest or Argo changes, so cluster risk is low, but capacity and alert evidence should be reviewed before any rollout that adds replicas or surge Pods. No approval is given here; hard guard rules remain in force.",
